# FinnOS base image — aarch64, the ARM dev machine.
#
# One package per line, as mkarchiso reads it; base/setup.sh reads the same
# file. The list is the x86_64 one with the ARM kernel and without the
# Intel microcode, which does not exist for a machine that is not an Intel
# machine.
#
# ARM boots through UEFI only, and it gets firmware from
# linux-firmware plus whatever the board ships in its own boot chain.

# The init system and the shell the disc boots into.
base
systemd
systemd-sysvcompat
sudo
util-linux
kbd

# The kernel, its firmware and the DRM/KMS stack the compositor drives.
linux-aarch64
linux-firmware
libdrm
libinput
seatd

# Mesa provides the GBM and EGL the accelerated path uses; libglvnd is the
# dispatch pkg-config's egl and glesv2 look for. Mesa's own dependencies
# name the `wayland` client library; it is not what pacman.conf refuses
# (that is the compositors), and this is why.
mesa
libglvnd

# What finn-comp links against.
freetype2
fontconfig
libwebp
alsa-lib
alsa-ucm-conf
ttf-dejavu

# The network, and a way in that is not the console.
networkmanager
openssh
curl

# The installer and the tools it needs.
arch-install-scripts
dosfstools
e2fsprogs
parted
gptfdisk

# GRUB is the bootloader on an ARM board; there is no syslinux and no BIOS
# boot partition there. The tools the machine that writes the disc needs
# are not on it: see "Building the medium" in README.md.
grub
efibootmgr

# Python for FinnSDK and the shell's tooling; git and the compiler because
# the machine builds the compositor from the sources the disc carries.
python
git
nano
vim
base-devel
pkgconf
# The local packages in base/pkgbuilds are deliberately not in this list:
# nothing on the disc installs from a repository that does not exist. The
# compositor and the SDK are built by the machine, from the sources.
